# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A-Network contracts — deploy parameters (NON-SECRET except the deployer key).
#
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Copy this file to `.env` (or append to your existing `.env`).
#   2. The deployer PRIVATE KEY must already be in `.env` as
#      DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY_BSC (mainnet) / DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY_BSC_TESTNET
#      (testnet). NEVER paste a private key into this example file.
#   3. Fill the TODO addresses (only needed for MAINNET; testnet defaults to the
#      deployer so you can dry-run the whole flow solo).
#   4. Deploy:
#        npm run deploy:l2portal:bsc-testnet
#        npm run deploy:feeproc:bsc-testnet
#      then, once verified on testnet:
#        npm run deploy:l2portal:bsc
#        npm run deploy:feeproc:bsc
#
# Everything below is read by scripts/deploy-l2-portal.js and
# scripts/deploy-fee-processor.js. Sensible defaults are applied when a value
# is omitted (see each script's header) — on TESTNET you can leave most blank.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Deployer key (SECRET — put the real key in .env, not here) ───────────────
# DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY_BSC=0x...            # BSC mainnet deployer
# DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY_BSC_TESTNET=0x...    # BSC testnet deployer (needed to deploy on testnet)

# ── Optional: verify on the explorer right after deploy ──────────────────────
# VERIFY_CONTRACT=true
# BSCSCAN_API_KEY=...

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# AnetL2Portal (canonical lock-and-mint BSC ⇆ L2 bridge)
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ANET BEP-20 token the portal locks. Mainnet default is the live ANET; on
# testnet you MUST supply a testnet ANET token address.
ANET_TOKEN=0x791055A7d52AA392eaE8De04250497f33807E46A

# L2 chain id native ANET lives on. Defaults: opBNB mainnet 204 / testnet 5611.
# L2_CHAIN_ID=204

# Admin (Gnosis Safe recommended) + separate cold pauser key.
# MAINNET: set these. TESTNET: omit to default to the deployer.
# PORTAL_ADMIN=0xTODO_SAFE_ADDRESS
# PORTAL_PAUSER=0xTODO_COLD_PAUSER

# M-of-N relayer signer set that authorizes L2→BSC withdrawals (EIP-712).
# Comma-separated addresses + the required threshold.
# MAINNET: set the real signer set. TESTNET: omit → deployer 1-of-1.
# PORTAL_SIGNERS=0xSigner1,0xSigner2,0xSigner3
# PORTAL_THRESHOLD=2

# Withdrawal caps (whole ANET). per-tx ≤ per-recipient-24h ≤ global-24h.
# PORTAL_MAX_PER_TX=1000
# PORTAL_MAX_RECIP_24H=5000
# PORTAL_MAX_GLOBAL_24H=20000

# Transparency pointers (set automatically post-deploy if admin == deployer).
# PORTAL_BSC_EXPLORER=https://bscscan.com/tx/
# PORTAL_L2_EXPLORER=https://opbnbscan.com/tx/
# PORTAL_BACKING_STATEMENT=L2 native ANET is 1:1 backed by ANET locked in this portal.

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# AnetFeeProcessor (ANET fees → BNB via the public PancakeSwap ANET/WBNB pool)
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PancakeSwap V2 router. Defaults by network:
#   mainnet 0x10ED43C718714eb63d5aA57B78B54704E256024E
#   testnet 0xD99D1c33F9fC3444f8101754aBC46c52416550D1
# PANCAKE_ROUTER=0x10ED43C718714eb63d5aA57B78B54704E256024E

# Fixed BNB destination for converted fees (Safe). TESTNET: omit → deployer.
# FEE_TREASURY=0xTODO_SAFE_ADDRESS

# Admin / pauser / operator. MAINNET: set. TESTNET: omit → deployer.
# FEE_ADMIN=0xTODO_SAFE_ADDRESS
# FEE_PAUSER=0xTODO_COLD_PAUSER
# FEE_OPERATOR=0xTODO_BACKEND_HOT_WALLET   # the bsc-relayer wallet that calls processFees

# Per-call ANET cap (whole ANET) + on-chain slippage tolerance (bps; 300 = 3%).
# FEE_MAX_PER_CALL=10000
# FEE_MAX_SLIPPAGE_BPS=300

# Transparency pointers (set automatically post-deploy if admin == deployer).
# FEE_BSC_EXPLORER=https://bscscan.com/tx/
# FEE_POOL_INFO=PancakeSwap V2 ANET/WBNB — converts ANET fees to BNB on the open market.
